id: pm-vcs-ci-disk-reserve
title: Apply Fleet CI v2 and remove repeated PR release gates
description: "Apply Fleet CI v2 for companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. Preserve required Linux and Windows checks, move four exhaustive release gates to isolated deep jobs, retain the self-host gate and unchanged coverage thresholds. Reuse the existing CI capacity task and retain its 20 GiB storage prerequisite."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[7]: ci,follow-up,"gh:unbraind/pm-vcs#151","gh:unbraind/pm-vcs#154","gh:unbraind/pm-vcs#209",infrastructure,performance
created_at: "2026-11-05T03:29:08.898Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-16T04:57:14.494Z"
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-vcs-tracker-admission
comments[34]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-15T13:11:29.225Z",codex-sol,"Reusing this CI capacity Task for Fleet CI v2, companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. Preserve all four required checks (test 22/26 and Windows launcher 22/26). One quick Node 26 npm release gate per PR replaces four full gates, removing sequential gate accumulation implicated in #154. Deep keeps all four full gates as isolated matrix jobs. Keep the 20 GiB guard and all coverage thresholds. Release caller rollout pm-ops#272 files are out of scope."
  "2026-11-15T13:18:12.191Z",codex-sol,"Latest successful main run 43609609072: test 22 execution 176m30s, test 26 93m03s; each ran npm and Bun gates. CLI combined-log download returned empty; direct jobs API log supplied evidence. Slowest lifecycle model 835s; large-history and exhaustive crash matrices also dominate. Added deterministic quick prefixes, propagated depth/time-scale through the child allowlist, scaled crash subprocess safety budgets and replaced the 512 TiB refusal speed assertion with a one-read bound. Existing annotation managed fixtures already await owned resources and retry removal (maxRetries 8); #151 is regression verification, not a newly reproduced fix. Coverage thresholds and all old gate contracts retained. Local quick coverage deferred because exhaustive matrices and historical runtime make the 20-minute budget implausible."
  "2026-11-15T13:19:19.949Z",codex-sol,"Strict YAML parsing with unique-key validation passed for all three tier workflows; actionlint is unavailable. Source typecheck, build, duplicates (0%), docstrings (616 declarations) and lint pass. Initial build:test ran before dist existed and failed on three pre-existing dist imports; source build has completed and the linked check is rerunning. Bounded focused quick tests and existing ENOTEMPTY lifecycle regressions are running."
  "2026-11-15T13:23:30.820Z",codex-sol,"PR #209 initial head 8bc8865 is queued in CI run 43718573852 and CodeQL run 43718573874. Committed self-host verification passed. The main log shows annotation history alone cost 427s and bisect history 146s per gate. Quick histories now use a 200-commit deterministic prefix; full retains 2000. Exact read budgets, unrelated-payload refusal, zero additional bisect reads, logarithmic decisions and every signature verdict remain asserted; focused verification is running before a follow-up push."
  "2026-11-15T13:27:56.853Z",codex-sol,"Follow-up validation: quick history read-budget and signature tests pass 3/3 through pm test in 197.04s; full defaults retain 2000 commits and original bounds. Workflow/depth tests pass 11/11 in 20.88s, including actual Bash classification, docs/tracker data, executable tracker code, source deletion accompanying a docs rename and unusual filenames. All fixture lifecycle regressions pass 7/7 with PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3 in 11.44s, preserving transient retries and persistent failure reporting. Test compilation and lint pass again. Initial committed self-host acceptance passed. Broader touched quick tests remain under their 20-minute ceiling."
  "2026-11-15T13:32:10.520Z",codex-sol,"Bounded touched quick run finished in 12m56.28s: 264 tests, 263 pass and one import-order audit failure caused by helper imports preceding isolate-session. Corrected import order in every touched entrypoint without weakening the audit. Targeted environment/isolation audit now passes 2/2 (144 entrypoints, 219 explicit child launch sites, six embedded workers), and workflow/depth tests pass 11/11 again in 12.34s. All seeded lifecycle, destruction, admission, diff and derivation assertions in the original focused run passed; no full local depth or coverage was attempted. Quick history regressions pass 3/3 and fixture lifecycle regressions pass 7/7 as previously recorded. Both committed self-host acceptance rounds pass. Changelog consistency and strict health pass with the workflow-pinned project extension and an isolated global profile. The ordinary local profile exposes the pre-existing global extension skew tracked by pm-vcs-5lre; no shared settings were changed."
  "2026-11-15T13:32:11.653Z",codex-sol,"Implementation handoff: PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/209 . Existing queued implementation run 43719295160 and CodeQL run 43719295147 will be superseded by the import-order correction. Watch budget ends 30 minutes after the initial PR run was created (13:51 UTC). Queue-inclusive completed-job wall times cannot yet be measured. Coverage at unchanged thresholds, complete quick PR runtime, deep full-depth runtime and native Windows execution remain CI evidence gaps. One gate per job removes #154 sequential accumulation; the preserved 20 GiB preflight may still reject insufficient runners. CodeQL is not required. Release workflow, pm-github workflows, verifier scripts, protection and variables remain untouched."
  "2026-11-15T14:24:09.057Z",codex-sol,"Round 2: fixing the supplied review findings, auditing the whole CI v2 diff for the same defect classes, and running the requested focused gates. Review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-11-15T14:29:19.386Z",codex-sol,"The gate-input audit retains self-host acceptance, packed documentation privacy, changelog date verification and Git identity auditing on the cheap Linux path. Tooling also exposed an unresolved matrix executable in deep CI; use explicit npm and Bun branches so the unchanged attestation gate can prove both commands."
  "2026-11-15T14:33:29.547Z",codex-sol,"Validation passed: typecheck, lint, build:test, 42 workflow/release-tooling tests through pm test --run --only-last --progress, all 64 self-host tests including stale README and tracker refusal, and strict workflow YAML parsing. The initial tooling run exposed the deep matrix executable expansion; explicit npm/Bun branches fixed it and the complete 42-test rerun passed. Self-host bundle must now be refreshed after the final tracker/changelog writes and verified on the committed head."
  "2026-11-15T14:40:13.908Z",codex-sol,"Committed-head verification passed self-host byte equality, real packed-file privacy (365 files, zero findings), and release changelog date verification. The combined linked command then failed on the known shared physical-object identity condition tracked by pm-vcs-identity-isolation; a fresh single-branch clone passed the unchanged identity gate with five approved addresses. Record this as an explicit local limitation, not a failed candidate ancestry or relaxed gate. Regenerate the bundle for these final evidence records and rerun committed acceptance before push."
  "2026-11-15T19:58:39.555Z",codex-sol-round-d,"Round D: inspecting assigned failing CI logs and complete PR diff; preserve append-only tracker history and all release/privacy contracts."
  "2026-11-15T20:19:52.810Z",codex-sol-round-d,"Round D: both Linux jobs in run 43725955802 exceeded the 30-minute limit. Logs show exhaustive native power/crash images still ran at quick depth; timeout cancellation then removed gate scratch and caused secondary ENOENT failures. Quick now executes the deterministic generated cut prefix (one tenth, at least 25), retaining complete trace/image enumeration comparisons and every original full-depth cut in deep. Completion counts and timing averages use selected outcomes only. Linked tests passed 22/22, no skips (305716 ms), including actual obliterate-packed recovery of 54/538 crash images across 832 native boundaries. Linked typecheck, build:test and lint passed. Strict unique-key YAML parsed nine files. Fixed fractional timeout rounding and validated fixture scale before spawn; disposable reverts fail both regressions and restore passes. PRRT_kwDOToJT7M63qwPz is valid: docs table and cheap-path prose now include Linux self-host, identity, packed privacy and date gates. Memory-backed acceleration was measured without establishing an improvement and was discarded. No covered source was edited; unchanged 100 percent quick coverage and sub-30-minute total duration still need exact-head CI. Stage these final records, regenerate selfhost.bundle, commit it and verify committed source equality before pushing. No review-thread actions or merge."
  "2026-11-15T20:20:19.107Z",codex-sol-round-d,"Correction to the preceding receipt: the real obliterate-packed run enumerated 5488 native boundaries, not 832; it recovered 54 selected images out of 538 generated distinct images. All other pass counts and timings in that receipt are unchanged."
  "2026-11-15T20:34:51.791Z",codex-sol-round-d,"Additional native-helper verification exceeded its 600-second local budget after purge-journal and retired-instance scenarios passed (79 and 82 cuts respectively); interrupted-unpack was still running, and storage-file cases had not started. This is missing complete evidence, not a pass. A ten-percent crash prefix is still too large: quick crash recovery is now capped at the first 25 generated cuts per scenario (or all if fewer); seeded-property testDepth remains unchanged and deep/default still executes every cut. Enumeration, retained-data assertions, completion counters and original 100 percent coverage thresholds remain intact. Rerun the affected native checks with two-CPU affinity and a bounded 900-second command."
  "2026-11-15T20:39:51.178Z",codex-sol-round-d,"Final 25-cut native verification passed through pm test --run --progress with two-CPU affinity: 55/55 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 240607.597 ms. Five real SIGKILL scenarios verified 25/788 purge-journal cuts, 25/818 retired-instance cuts, 25/1018 interrupted-unpack cuts, 9/9 scan-publication cuts, and 25/118 proof-denial cuts: 109 actual selected cuts total. All complete trace comparisons, retained-data/foreign-file assertions and completion guards passed. The stored test link remained at its existing 600-second bound because repeated --add is idempotent; the final applied runtime bound was 600 seconds, not the planned 900. Fresh typecheck, build:test and lint passed; final helper/fixture tests passed 11/11 in 9158 ms. Final 25-case prefix, integer rounding and before-spawn validation reverts fail and restore passes. The earlier ten-percent timeout remains recorded as incomplete evidence. No coverage source/threshold change, local coverage run or exact-head CI approval is claimed."
  "2026-11-15T22:24:26.966Z",codex-sol,"Round E: verified assigned review findings and current checks. Fix valid portability, gate-order and timeout regressions; preserve product deadlines, privacy/identity and self-host gates. Run targeted quick tests and required tooling checks before an explicit-path commit. Review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-11-15T22:37:59.013Z",codex-sol,"Round E evidence: Both assigned checks hit the 30-minute job timeout. The Node 26 log measures 474 and 504 seconds for two benchmark tests: each redundantly runs both in-process and CLI benchmarks, resulting in four full executions. Retain one direct benchmark and one real CLI invocation from a checkout containing spaces. Keep every source and coverage threshold intact. Targeted benchmark/fixture validation is running."
  "2026-11-15T22:45:21.314Z",codex-sol,"Round E direct targeted check: PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/cdc-benchmark.test.ts test/depth.test.ts test/fixture-lifetime.test.ts; running; final result will be checked before push. No package coverage sources were changed; no package coverage run was performed."
  "2026-11-15T22:50:10.661Z",codex-sol,"Round E final verification: typecheck, lint (docstring gate where no lint script exists), touched regression tests, workflow/tooling tests, strict workflow YAML and changelog:check passed. Duplication gates passed where provided. Self-review retained docs/tracker privacy and identity checks, unscaled product deadlines, integer-rounded validated harness budgets, platform filename guards and generated-only quick thresholds. No package coverage sources were edited; no package coverage run. No review thread actions or merge. Shared-runner hold and SteveBot commit identity will be checked before push. Hosted CI is intentionally not awaited. Benchmark/depth/fixture batch passed 14/14 in 1217208 ms on the shared host; workflow/tooling batch passed 25/25. Regenerate selfhost.bundle from the staged source and verify the committed archive before push."
  "2026-11-16T00:22:55.341Z",codex-sol,"Round F: verify assigned review findings and failing Actions checks, audit related tier contracts, add regressions, run focused gates and push without waiting for CI. Review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-11-16T00:35:31.520Z",codex-sol,"Round F: PRRT_kwDOToJT7M63uyRS is valid. New routing tests now isolate first and use explicit fixture environments; every new rollout test file was audited. The failed ordinary batch suppressed all serial tests and produced most coverage shortfalls. Keep running both batches while preserving failure status, with a regression. Node 22 uses the existing complete batched runner to address its 30-minute serial timeout. Preserve benchmark CLI coverage through its spaced-path alias. Self-review also restores CodeQL for executable tracker programs. Focused isolation audit passed: 146 entrypoints and 221 launches. No coverage source changed."
  "2026-11-16T00:46:44.434Z",codex-sol,"Refinement: retain the separate spaced-checkout benchmark fixture unchanged. Run the complete benchmark through the original CLI entrypoint with runner instrumentation preserved, covering its previously missed main guard. The final isolation audit passes all 146 test entrypoints and 222 child launches; PM-linked routing, workflow, CodeQL and batch regression checks pass all 17 tests."
  "2026-11-16T00:54:17.039Z",codex-sol,"Final local gates pass: typecheck, lint, test compilation, 17 PM-linked routing/workflow/batch tests, 10 quality-script tests, the real complete benchmark CLI, strict YAML, changelog consistency and the complete isolation audit. The benchmark CLI passed in about 463 seconds at quick depth. No coverage source changed; no local coverage was run. Stage the tracked source and tracker, regenerate selfhost.bundle, then verify the committed archive with accept:self-host before pushing. New CI runtime and full coverage remain for the orchestrator."
  "2026-11-16T02:22:47.712Z",codex-sol,"Quick-fit follow-up: cancelled required checks reached the unchanged 30-minute ceiling without a test failure. Audit exhaustive boundary, compiler and consumer matrices; retain deterministic kind coverage in quick and complete enumeration in deep. Compare focused local quick timings, then measure PR job steps within the 30-minute post-push observation window. Product timing contracts and coverage thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-16T02:29:35.267Z",codex-sol,"Finite quick selection now keeps 25 of 700 resolution schedules with explicit reader/transition/boundary set assertions; pinned and SIGKILL traces keep every named boundary kind; pending roots keep all 6 formats in both representations; lifecycle keeps 25 deterministic seeds and existing crash/payload coverage assertions. One project-installed composition consumer, one real-host raw resolution and one instrumented complete CDC benchmark remain quick; all other combinations remain deep. Typecheck and test compilation pass; lint and focused timing runs are in progress. Regenerate committed self-host bundle after staging all final inputs."
  "2026-11-16T02:32:04.586Z",codex-sol,"Reader follow-up: added a dedicated inventory interruption, for 26 quick schedules total. Assert actually injected boundary and transition sets, so the selection cannot pass on merely named but unreachable schedules. Typecheck, test compilation, lint and 4 depth-helper tests pass (including pm test --run --only-last --progress). The focused old/new quick commands remain in progress; no local full-depth run is attempted."
  "2026-11-16T02:38:32.634Z",codex-sol,"Additional ranked Node 22 hotspot: packed move-source consumers took 92.889s before this change. Quick now retains the Node SDK path with every source-eligibility and snapshot-ownership scenario; all Node/Bun × SDK/JSON/TOON combinations remain deep. The direct real-host conflict and composition representatives remain quick. Frozen before/after extra-consumer runs are started. The strengthened 26-schedule reader test passes in 149.401s under heavy shared load, including actual injection coverage assertions."
  "2026-11-16T02:41:21.876Z",codex-sol,"Expanded consumer selection passes test compilation, focused lint and the full entrypoint/embedded-worker isolation audit (1/1, 36.648s); allowlist instrumentation checks pass 2/2. Quick snapshot packed Node SDK consumer passes all 3 ownership scenarios in 59.624s. The unchanged complete benchmark reached its local 600s harness watchdog under load above 50, so the touched suite has a known local timeout; a PM-runner retry uses existing PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3 only for the harness. Product timing contracts and CI job ceilings are unchanged. Superseded bundle verification was stopped after additional tracked inputs changed; the final committed bundle will be regenerated and independently verified."
  "2026-11-16T03:07:35.338Z",codex-sol,"Bounded final quick-fit snapshot for code head 4464c11: the 15-minute target is NOT met. Linux jobs remain running after more than 20 minutes; Windows succeeds in 76s and 98s created-to-completed. Completed steps and running-step lower bounds are recorded below. Local quick paired results: composition consumers 1875.103s -> 758.688s (both pass); lifecycle 52 -> 25 seeds 982.711s -> 632.793s (both pass, all 8 crash kinds and 4 payload pairs); move consumer 332.659s watchdog -> 137.713s pass; snapshot consumer 332.624s watchdog -> 59.624s pass. New raw-value CLI path passes in 401.994s; reader resolution passes in 113.600s and pinned retirement in 444.993s. The full touched-file run stops with 48 passes, one unchanged benchmark watchdog failure and 3 cancelled files. Its scale-3 benchmark retry passes 1/1 through the PM runner in 1335.744s. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, workflow YAML, 4 depth tests and environment audits pass. Source bundle at code head 4464c11 independently verified byte-identical; the receipt bundle will be regenerated and verified after committing these final inputs. Coverage preservation and complete CI remain unverified. Remaining work includes named-kind selection for the 25-cut lifecycle/fixture/journal helper prefixes, plus prior-log generated histories 102.111s, root spellings 70.303s, large-history metadata 68.900s, large logical descriptors 68.322s, JSON header repair 58.555s and other packed conflict-format consumers. Exact new-run ranking needs completed logs. Detailed commands and timings: docs/ci-quick-fit-measurements.md. Release the claim, keep in_progress, never close.\n\n# Quick-fit measurements: pm-vcs\n\nCode head: `4464c113add64c3aa48e4724dd5d72759d46bf2e`. [CI run 43794135980](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/43794135980).\nJobs API snapshot: 2026-11-16T03:06:25+00:00. All local timing commands use `PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick`; unset/full depth is not run locally.\n\n| Job | Result at snapshot | Created to completion | Queue | Started to completion |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| test (26) | in_progress | unfinished | 1s | >= 1219s running |\n| test (22) | in_progress | unfinished | 1s | >= 1219s running |\n| windows-acceptance-launcher (22) | success | 76s | 1s | 75s |\n| windows-acceptance-launcher (26) | success | 98s | 2s | 96s |\n\nStep times are completed wall times from `started_at` to `completed_at`; running values are lower bounds, not completed durations.\n\n| Step | test (26) | test (22) | windows-acceptance-launcher (22) | windows-acceptance-launcher (26) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Set up job | 3s success | 1s success | 1s success | 1s success |\n| Checkout | 17s success | 14s success | 19s success | 21s success |\n| Detect code changes | 0s success | 0s success | 0s success | 0s success |\n| Setup Node.js | 4s success | 1s success | 7s success | 12s success |\n| Setup Bun | 0s success | 1s success | — | — |\n| Install dependencies | 4s success | 4s success | 16s success | 14s success |\n| Install project pm-github extension | 0s success | 1s success | 2s success | 6s success |\n| Verify tracked pm project health | 1s success | 1s success | 2s success | 2s success |\n| Check documentation and tracker changes | skipped | skipped | skipped | skipped |\n| Engines floor build and quick tests | skipped | >= 1195s running | — | — |\n| Quick npm release gate | >= 1189s running | pending | — | — |\n| Keep the coverage report when the gate fails | pending | pending | — | — |\n| Bun and bunx install smoke | pending | pending | — | — |\n| Post Setup Bun | pending | pending | — | — |\n| Post Setup Node.js | pending | pending | 1s success | 1s success |\n| Post Checkout | pending | pending | 2s success | 2s success |\n| Verify the installed PM CLI launcher | — | — | 2s success | 1s success |\n| Build Windows storage acceptance | — | — | 1s success | 1s success |\n| Verify Windows GC apply on a non-git tracker | — | — | 20s success | 34s success |\n| Complete job | — | — | 0s success | 0s success |"
  "2026-11-16T04:23:33.740Z",codex-sol,"Resuming the interrupted round G under the requested handoff. Reviewed the pending tracker changes. Implementing separate Node 22 shards, Node 26 coverage shards and exact hit union, plus non-coverage gates with required success aggregates. CI will provide timing and merged coverage evidence; thresholds and deep gates stay unchanged."
  "2026-11-16T04:38:20.819Z",codex-sol,"Implementation ready for hosted measurement: ten Node 22 quick shards, ten Node 26 coverage shards, a parallel non-coverage release gate, offset-aware c8 coverage merge and required test (22/26) aggregates. The Windows acceptance launcher job block is byte-for-byte unchanged. V8 raw offset merging is required: the fixture caught an extra branch when converting to Istanbul before merging; merging through the original c8 reporter matches unsharded totals and boolean hit maps. Source hashes and runtime versions bind artifacts; missing/duplicate/mismatched shards fail closed. Existing --all --100 --per-file source scope and all four thresholds stay unchanged. Workflow/routing/merge tests passed 7/7 via pm test; source inventory and original c8 command controls passed 2/2. Typecheck, build:test, lint, zero-duplication gate, docstrings and changelog check passed. Focused coverage of the new gate is 100% lines/branches/functions/statements; Node 26 fixture passed. This is not full-suite coverage. Hosted times and merged full-suite coverage remain pending. Regenerating the self-host bundle from staged source and tracker inputs before commit; verification will read the committed result."
  "2026-11-16T04:41:07.682Z",codex-sol,"Refined the shard count from actual completed-test timings before relying on the new CI run: the prior Node 26 log provides file evidence for 81 of 148 files. Ten-way sorted assignment has a 1038 s known maximum; fourteen-way assignment reduces it to 692 s plus setup and the unfinished tail. Increased both matrices to fourteen shards to fit the projected target. Workflow contracts and test compilation pass after the count change. The tail remains a timing risk for hosted CI, not a completed measurement."
  "2026-11-16T04:57:12.776Z",codex-sol,"Hosted run 43805767467 exposed two integration gaps: the production durability audit rejects direct rmSync in the new merge gate, and dependency-refresh-workflow contracts assumed the old job layout and YAML presentation. Changed cleanup to durability.discardTemporary and made the contracts parse YAML and exercise the actual release and coverage wrappers while preserving their storage/cleanup assertions. Focused workflow tests pass 10/10; durability audit passes; typecheck/build:test, lint, zero duplication and docstrings pass. No durability bypass or source exclusion was added. The full coverage merge remains unmeasured because two prior shards failed these integration assertions. Rebuilding the committed self-host bundle with this repair."
